      "title": "Lecturer in Philosophy",
      "description": "AHCPR1088 Lecturer in Philosophy - Jobs at the University of Leeds Skip to main content Home Login Register Current Vacancies How to Apply Criminal records Working at Leeds Contact Us FAQs Terms and conditions Terms of use Contact us Accessibility Privacy Cookies Freedom of information Cookies This site requires the use of cookies as defined by our Terms and Conditions . \r\n        We have provided a detailed description of how cookies work and are used on the site . \r\n        To accept cookies, please click the \"Accept Cookies\" button. Accept Cookies Home Login Register Current Vacancies How To Apply Criminal records Working at Leeds Contact Us FAQs Lecturer in Philosophy Are you an ambitious researcher in Philosophy with the ability to carry out world-leading research and deliver an exceptional student experience in a research-intensive Russell Group University? Would you like to join and contribute to a vibrant philosophical community within the interdisciplinary School of Philosophy, Religion and History of Science? The School of Philosophy, Religion, and History of Science at the University of Leeds is seeking an outstanding philosopher with research expertise and teaching experience in moral and/or political philosophy, understood to comprise metanormative theory, moral psychology, normative ethics, political philosophy, and legal philosophy. The successful candidate will lead or direct their own original and independent programme of research at an international standard. The philosophical community within the School is one of the largest and most vibrant in the UK. We have particular research strengths in metaphysics, epistemology, philosophy of science, philosophy of mind, aesthetics, ethics, and political philosophy. Research activity in the area of this post is supported by the Centre for Aesthetic, Moral and Political Philosophy (CAMP). The School has the ambition to be a dynamic and welcoming community renowned for both its academic excellence and its impact on policy, practice, and public life. We value an inclusive working and learning environment and our aim is to develop a diverse staff and student community reflective of this. In addition to the standard online application form that covers the above essential and desirable criteria, please upload the following (in this order) as a single PDF: A standard academic CV; A description of future research plans (1-2 pages), e.g. elaboration of research projects, future publication plans, and/or grant application plans; A recent research writing sample (maximum 10,000 words); *Interviews are to take place on 10 and 11 February 2027* What we offer in return 26 days holiday plus approx.16 Bank Holidays/days that the University is closed by custom (including Christmas) – That’s 42 days a year! Generous pension scheme plus life assurance– the University contributes 14.5% of salary Health and Wellbeing: Discounted staff membership options at The Edge, our state-of-the-art Campus gym, with a pool, sauna, climbing wall, cycle circuit, and sports halls. Personal Development: Access to courses run by our Organisational Development & Professional Learning team. Access to on-site childcare, shopping discounts and travel schemes are also available. And much more! To explore the post further or for any queries you may have, please contact: Prof Pekka Väyrynen, Deputy Head of School (Philosophy and History of Science). Email: p.vayrynen@leeds.ac.uk Email details to a friend Apply Online Share: View All Vacancies Job Details Location Leeds - Main Campus Faculty/Service Faculty of Arts, Humanities & Cultures School/Institute School of Philosophy, Religion & History of Science Category Academic Grade Grade 8 Salary £51,753 to £59,966\r\n              p.a. Working Time 100% Post Type Full Time Contract Type Ongoing Release Date Thursday 15 October 2026 Closing Date Sunday 22 November 2026 Reference AHCPR1088 Downloads Candidate Brief (PDF) Apply Online Search